# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# The app is a client-side SPA: /search, /builder and /compare/:id exist only in
# the router, not as files on disk. Without this rule a hard refresh on any
# sub-route returns Netlify's 404 instead of index.html.
#
# 200 = rewrite (serve index.html), NOT 301 = redirect, so the browser keeps the
# real URL and the router can render the right page.

# /api/* is a serverless function (the Gemini proxy), never the SPA. Rules are
# evaluated top-down and the first match wins, so this MUST come before the
# catch-all — otherwise a POST to /api/ai/... gets index.html with a 200 and the
# AI fails with a JSON parse error instead of reaching the proxy.
/api/*    200

/*    /index.html   200

# Never rewrite the static asset folders — they must 404 properly if missing.
/assets/*  /assets/:splat  200
